.vscode/**
.vscode-test/**
src/**
tests/**
.github/**
.gitignore
.vscodeignore
justfile
.bumpversion.toml
RELEASE.md
REUSE.toml
tsconfig.json
tsconfig.host-test.json
esbuild.js
vitest.config.mts
# Dev tooling with no runtime purpose. These configure the linters and test
# runners used to BUILD the extension; a user's install has no linter and no
# test runner to configure, so they were shipping 5 KB of noise to every seat.
.markdownlint.json
.pre-commit-config.yaml
optimize-gif.js
eslint.config.mjs
package-lock.json
node_modules/**
.pytest_cache/**
# The other two tool caches, and the reason they need naming when
# .pytest_cache did not: all three are invisible to `git status` here because a
# GLOBAL gitignore covers them, and a global gitignore protects git and nothing
# else. `vsce package` does not read it. So .mypy_cache/ -- 8.9 MB of type-stub
# data -- was being packaged into every install, while every manifest and every
# status command in the repository looked clean. Found by noticing an
# unexplained 445 KB jump in the VSIX and listing what it actually contained.
.mypy_cache/**
.ruff_cache/**
# Build configuration with no runtime purpose, same category as the linter
# configs above: a user's install has no npm to configure.
.npmrc
# The root-level unit test. `**/*.ts` above already excludes its only file, so
# this changes nothing today and states the intent rather than relying on a
# glob that happens to cover it.
test/**
*.vsix
**/*.ts
**/*.map
.architect/**
# Gitignored locally, so a CI build (which packages a clean git checkout)
# never sees them — but a local `vsce package` does, and would ship internal
# governance material and a coverage report to every Marketplace user.
.claude/**
.gemini/**
.human/**
.zenzic-score.json
.zenzic-history.jsonl
.DS_Store
coverage/**
.zenzic_cache/**
example/**
_zenzic_core/**
# A local Python virtualenv at the repository root. CI never has one here (it
# syncs the core into _zenzic_core/, excluded above), so CI's VSIX is clean and
# its 5 MB size guard never fired -- but `vsce package` run on a developer
# machine that has one would ship every file in it. Found by listing what the
# packaged VSIX actually contains rather than trusting the guard that had never
# been given the chance to fail.
.venv/**
# Compiled extension-host test code. `tests/**` and `tsconfig.host-test.json`
# are already excluded above; this is the same material after `tsc`, and it
# additionally carries a runtime `require('glob')` that resolves only through a
# devDependency. The suite runs from the working tree, never from the VSIX.
out/test/**
# The demo-capture sandbox is build/marketing tooling, not extension runtime.
# Unlike the entries above it is committed, but a Marketplace user has no use
# for it and it would ship a Dockerfile inside every install. Being tracked and
# being packaged are different questions: this file and .gitignore are separate
# manifests, and neither one implies the other.
docker/**
# The recording scratch directory, and the reason it needs its own line: it is
# in .gitignore, and .gitignore is not .vscodeignore. `vsce package` on a
# developer machine that has just regenerated the demo packaged 1.8 MB of it --
# the MP4 intermediate, six probe frames and a duplicate of the GIF -- into
# every install. Found by hashing what the VSIX actually contains rather than
# by reading either manifest. Same shape as the .venv/** entry above.
.demo-out/**
# The demo asset's verification gate. Build/marketing tooling like docker/**
# and optimize-gif.js, both excluded above; a Marketplace user has no GIF to
# verify.
scripts/**
ROADMAP.md
# images/demo*.gif was excluded here by the v0.23.3 package-optimisation
# pass, before any such file existed. The demo GIF now exists, and unlike the
# internal entries above it is public marketing content, so it ships with the
# package: well under a tenth of the 5 MB CI ceiling on a 256 KB baseline.
# Deliberate inclusion, not an oversight.
